To manually select your desired intensity, press the intensity indicator lights on the handle, to cycle through the options. The intensity setting can be changed before, during, or after brushing.


<PIC:toothbrush0_07>
{{image description: Toothbrush handle with mode/intensity indicator dots; arrows and labels x1, x2, x3 show cycling through three levels by pressing the button.}}

Your toothbrush measures the motions while brushing to detect scrubbing behavior (see brushing instructions for optimal technique). If you regularly scrub while brushing, the app will recommend that you enable Scrubbing Feedback. When Scrubbing Feedback is activated the brushing feedback light at the bottom of the handle will illuminate amber and the handle will change its vibration as a reminder to stop scrubbing. The brushing feedback light will turn off when you stop scrubbing. Note: Scrubbing Feedback comes deactivated. To activate this feature, see 'Activating or deactivating features'.


<PIC:Manual37_10>
{{image description: Person brushing teeth with the toothbrush at the mouth and a curved arrow at the handle showing brushing movement.}}

2. Place the charging stand (clear cover) on the charging base.
<PIC:Manual37_14>
{{image description: USB charging adapter and cable diagram; arrow 1 points to plugging the cable into the adapter and arrow 2 shows plugging the adapter into a wall outlet.}}

3. Place the toothbrush handle on the charger.
<PIC:Manual37_15>
{{image description: Charging base diagram with a charging cup or holder being placed downward onto the base.}}




<PIC:Manual37_16>
{{image description: Toothbrush handle being placed downward into a charging cup/base; a black arrow shows insertion.}}

4. Leave the toothbrush on the charger until it is fully charged. The battery light will turn off (stop blinking) when the handle has finished charging.


<PIC:Manual37_17>
{{image description: Toothbrush standing in a charging base with starburst symbols indicating charging lights.}}

3. Place toothbrush into travel case.
<PIC:Manual37_18>
{{image description: USB cable being inserted into the end of a travel case or charger; a black arrow points toward the port.}}




<PIC:Manual37_19>
{{image description: Travel case opened with a toothbrush handle inside; arrows show placing the handle into the case and routing or closing a cable area.}}

4. Leave travel case plugged in until toothbrush is fully charged. The battery light will turn off (stop blinking) when the handle has finished charging.
<PIC:Manual37_20>
{{image description: Travel case or charger connected to a cable, with starburst charging indicators on top.}}




<PIC:Manual37_21>
{{image description: Travel case lying on a surface with a check mark, indicating correct charging or storage orientation.}}

When the handle is placed on the charger or in the travel case, the battery indication will communicate the battery level.


<PIC:Manual37_22>
{{image description: Battery status table: Charging blinks in white; Full illuminates white for 30 seconds and then turns off.}}

When the toothbrush is awake, the battery light at the bottom of the handle will indicate the status of the battery.


<PIC:Manual37_23>
{{image description: Battery status table showing Full, Partially full, Low, and Empty; indications include illuminated white, blinking white, blinking amber, and beeps after brushing.}}

The brush heads and handle can be cleaned by rinsing it with warm water.

1. Remove the brush head from the handle and rinse it thoroughly.


2. Rinse the entire handle, especially the brush head connection. Gently clean around the rubber seal. At least once a week.
<PIC:toothbrush0_08>
{{image description: Toothbrush head being rinsed under running water while a hand holds the brush head near the bristles.}}




<PIC:toothbrush0_09>
{{image description: Toothbrush handle shaft being rinsed under running water after removing the brush head.}}


Note: Do not push on the rubber seal at the top of the handle.


<PIC:toothbrush0_10>
{{image description: Incorrect cleaning diagram with a large X; a tool or brush is inserted near the handle seal or shaft area, indicating not to clean that way.}}

